    "senderName": "NWS La Crosse WI",
    "headline": "Flood Warning issued September 20 at 6:54PM CDT until September 21 at 12:00AM CDT by NWS La Crosse WI",
    "description": "* WHAT...Flooding along the Root River due to excessive rainfall.\n\n* WHERE...Northern Fillmore County in southeastern Minnesota...\n\n* WHEN...Until midnight CDT tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of low-lying and flood-prone locations is\noccurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 648 PM CDT, minor flooding continues along the Root River in\nnorthern Fillmore County. The crest continues working downstream\nthis evening, falling from west to east tonight.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nRushford, Lanesboro, Rushford Village, Peterson and Whalan.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
    "instruction": "Be especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
